  "notes": [
    "Assumes the OBO mapping of docs/architecture.md as implemented by @kgdiff/formats: [Term] stanzas are nodes ([Typedef] stanzas only name relations); is_a and relationship: lines are edges whose predicate is the tag (is_a) or the relation id as written (part_of, located_in, has_symptom); is_obsolete → deprecated; replaced_by → replacedBy; synonym → aliases and also attrs.synonyms (\"text (SCOPE)\"), so synonym edits appear in both aliasChanges and attrChanges; other tags (def, namespace, xref, comment, consider, subset, created_by, creation_date…) → attrs.",
    "Obsolete terms stay in the file (OBO practice), so merge sources and the split source are modified, not removed. Their is_a / relationship edges are dropped; edges already present on the survivor become collapsed, new ones on the survivor are carried (retarget, cause merge).",
    "The split MHD:0000067 → MHD:0000204 + MHD:0000205 is heuristic: OBO consider: is not a kgdiff hint. It is detectable because the new term labels were NARROW synonyms of the obsoleted term (name evidence 1.0; the new terms also carry the old name as a RELATED synonym) and they take over its edges (carry-over 4/4 and 3/4 of the old term's edges, 4/6 and 3/5 of the new terms' edges). Treat a miss as a warning. The edges of the source and targets are listed under edges.uncertain: their status and edge facets (retarget cause split, or plain add / remove) depend on whether and how the split is detected.",
    "Obsoleted terms lose their is_a parents; per docs/algorithms.md §4 that is part of the obsoletion and yields no move facet. The merge sources carry a replacement facet (replacedBy added); the split source only gains consider: (an attribute), so it has none.",
    "attrChanges list keys only, because the exact value shape of OBO tags (def text with or without its xref list, multi-valued tags as arrays) is parser-defined."
  ],
